.TH KINTSUGI-MEMORY 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-memory \- lessons and skills search
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi memory
add "<lesson>" [\-\-models a,b] [\-\-source ...]
.br
.B kintsugi memory
search "<query>" [\-\-k N]
.br
.B kintsugi memory
reindex
.br
.B kintsugi memory
list
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage lessons and skills. Lessons are stored in .kintsugi/learned.md and
indexed for full-text search.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP \fBadd\fR
Append a lesson
.IP \fBsearch\fR
Search lessons and skills (FTS5)
.IP \fBreindex\fR
Rebuild the derived index
.IP \fBlist\fR
Show all lessons
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-models\fR
Comma-separated model list (add)
.IP \fB\-\-source\fR
Source reference (add)
.IP \fB\-\-k\fR
Number of results (search, default 8)
.SH EXAMPLES
Add a lesson:
.PP
  $ kintsugi memory add "always use context managers for file I/O"
.PP
Search lessons:
.PP
  $ kintsugi memory search "file handling"
.PP
Rebuild index:
.PP
  $ kintsugi memory reindex
.PP
List all lessons:
.PP
  $ kintsugi memory list
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-recall (1)
